{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born","id":945204,"title":"Honestly, though... should all things be equal? (Homid-born)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-06T18:33:07-07:00","id":945204,"title":"Honestly, though... should all things be equal? (Homid-born)","content":"I understand that it's a game and blah blah blah.... but let's be honest for a minute. Does it make sense that a 2 year old Lupus or an 8 year old Metis start with the same number of ability dots as an 18 year old human who's probably had 12 years of education, and possibly even a job or two by now?<br /> <br /> Given that the other breeds have generally better gifts and higher starting Gnosis (which DOES make sense... but we're talking 4 or 8 Freebie points of value, here), do you think Homid should get some kind of bump for the sake of balance and/or realism?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:07:30-07:00","id":945245,"title":"","content":"First, not necessarily 18 years old for homid. Garou very likely change around puberty, so possibly a few years earlier than that. And from first change to starting character (rank 1) is a ways down the line. Somewhere between a few months to a couple of years depending on the game. It's in that time, training to get to rank 1 that I figure Garou pick up a bunch of their skill points (putting them above the 11/7/4 of kinfolk).<br /> <br /> That being said...eh. I don't have a problem with it. The animal breeds should naturally have higher ratings in a number of abilities (athletics, primal urge, brawl and survival come to mind off the top of my head) and so this distribution works out fine.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't agree that other breeds get better gifts than homids.<br /> Oh...and from my experience, most players play homids anyways, so they can't be too unfavorably unbalanced I would think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-06T20:19:28-07:00","id":945250,"title":"","content":"A homid going through first change at 18 is considered rather late, though canonically there are later bloomers. Generally a starting character in no way represents a cub That's why they have 3 gifts.. I'd be prone to cut down the stats on cubs though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T05:21:53-07:00","id":945411,"title":"","content":"oh curious, if it ever comes up, when should the curse start to kick in, how many years ahead of the first change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T05:25:32-07:00","id":945412,"title":"","content":"The difference is that Homid have a way easier time functioning in human society than Lupus have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:15:36-07:00","id":945447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=945411#post945411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious, if it ever comes up, when should the curse start to kick in, how many years ahead of the first change?</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually put them hand in hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:51:03-07:00","id":945455,"title":"","content":"a lot of fluff descriptions, suggest the curse starts to take effect months or years before the firsting, is 2 - 3 years a good offhand guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:58:15-07:00","id":945460,"title":"","content":"And for the question on Homid cubs, remember lupus pick up a lot of things like primal urge, brawl, and dodge &quot;Naturally&quot; <br /> <br /> Which helps smooth over the seeming absurdity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T07:58:46-07:00","id":945461,"title":"","content":"Could be. Honestly, whatever works for your story (unhelpful I know). The books are pretty vague on the details here because it isn't something the players generally deal with.<br /> The way I see it, puberty and the Change go together and so if you throw the Curse in there, just have it begin building up at the start of puberty. It's going to last several years anyway so that will give you the lead time you need over the Change.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T11:06:56-07:00","id":945553,"title":"","content":"Agree, the curse starts as you hit puberty. Later on your curse leads to a strong emotional, dramatic event in your life or you get found by other werewolf first who induce it and voila - you change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T01:46:28-07:00","id":946019,"title":"","content":"I usually rule, that in character backgrounds the Curse should start with the First Change, at the latest. Usually it becomes evident before that. However, I usually explain new players, that the Curse increases gradually, and is not from zero at maximum over night.<br /> Game mechanics require in tabletop, that a Ahroun always has at least 5 Rage at character creation, which is usually just after the Rite of Passage. A fact that has been discussed a lot in these forums (and the forums on the old White Wolf Page). We'll see if the character creation process is changed in that regard in the next edition of the game...<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the 13/9/5 or 11/7/4 abilities. Lupus are limited on what they are allowed to choose, leading to higher stats in seemingly &quot;inherent&quot; abilities, like Primal-Urge or Brawl.<br /> So, for our larp we have a all-xp-based creation system, that makes this differences obsolete. Also, we usually don't allow lupus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 08-08-2016, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T14:57:05-07:00","id":946482,"title":"","content":"This is an issue damn near EVERY game system i have encountered have. Character's being the same whether someone's playing a 8 yr old kid, or a 58 yr old grizzled veteran having the same 'starting stat/points/dots' etc as everyone else..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T21:33:07-07:00","id":946734,"title":"","content":"I have trouble imagining a being with human-like intelligence being only 2 or 3 years old and having mastery of a human language as well as the ability to fully act as an adult, much less having the same set of skills that a young adult human has. Perhaps it would be more realistic to assume that any Lupus in a group of Garou is a bit older than the first change and has had some time to learn about human ways so that they aren't the human mental equivalent of toddlers. <br /> <br /> From a balance perspective, maybe they should lack a few skills to make up for having a Gnosis of 5 to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T02:19:21-07:00","id":946819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=946734#post946734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have trouble imagining a being with human-like intelligence being only 2 or 3 years old and having mastery of a human language as well as the ability to fully act as an adult, much less having the same set of skills that a young adult human has. Perhaps it would be more realistic to assume that any Lupus in a group of Garou is a bit older than the first change and has had some time to learn about human ways so that they aren't the human mental equivalent of toddlers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is said, that the human-like intelligence explodes in their minds after the first change. From that point on, several garou traits are active that weren't before. Healing, shape shifting, stepping sideways and ageing like a human.<br /> So, lupus born garou (and to a lesser degree metis born) were garou all their live, but developed into adolescence rather rapidly.<br /> <br /> So, the human-like intelligence doesn't develop over 2 or 3 years, but really in an instant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T05:24:54-07:00","id":946879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=945460#post945460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for the question on Homid cubs, remember lupus pick up a lot of things like primal urge, brawl, and dodge &quot;Naturally&quot;<br /> <br /> Which helps smooth over the seeming absurdity.</div> </div> </div> </div>But do Lupus-born have high stats in a lot of these because they're lupus, or do they have high stats because they still get full ability dots and have nowhere else to put them? I can't help but wonder how much of this thought process was reverse-engineered from a decade or two of gameplay.<br /> <br /> Remember with dots- a little goes a long way. Sure, wolves are faster than humans. That's why that form gets bonus physical attributes and a x2 running modifier. So a wolf that runs a lot shouldn't be sporting significantly more athletics than a human that runs a lot. Same for Brawl. Does a handful of territorial disputes and dominance displays over the course of 2 years of life really put the lupus on par with a professional boxer or MMA fighter in homid form? It's a big deal to have more than 2 dots in an ability... a 3 is a level of competence on par with a Master's Degree or a seasoned professional. A 4 means someone is as good at something as you're likely to meet in a normal person's life, because 5 is an olympic-level, 'one of the best on the planet'-scale ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=946819#post946819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is said, that the human-like intelligence explodes in their minds after the first change. From that point on, several garou traits are active that weren't before. Healing, shape shifting, stepping sideways and ageing like a human.<br /> So, lupus born garou (and to a lesser degree metis born) were garou all their live, but developed into adolescence rather rapidly.<br /> <br /> So, the human-like intelligence doesn't develop over 2 or 3 years, but really in an instant.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But a big questions is &quot;How much intelligence is that worth?&quot; Even assuming most Garou can't/don't finish High School, does the first change impart a Lupus with something actually comparable to 8 hours of education a day, 180+ days a year, for 10-12 years? Sure, we know Lupus can't start with Drive or Firearms or Computers/Technology/etc without spending freebie points... But can they do multiplication? Do they know what bacteria are, how longitude works, that there are seven continents, what lightning is, or what a kidney does? Homid-born from developed nations are sporting somewhere in the vicinity of 15,000 hours of education on very fundamental things that weren't considered even remotely obvious as little as a few centuries ago, and there is so much more to a Homid upbringing than simply understanding the nuances of human society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T06:30:53-07:00","id":946910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=946879#post946879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But a big questions is &quot;How much intelligence is that worth?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exact the level of Intelligence and Wits the player spend dots in. That said, lupus can't have...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Restricted Abilities: Beginning lupus characters cannot take the following Skills and Knowledges. You may, however, use freebie points to purchase them, perhaps as a result of your character\u2019s prelude. Similarly, you can use experience points to add these Abilities as a result of \u201ctraining\u201d in the course of the chronicle (which is a chance for Storytellers with a sharp sense of humor to have some devilish fun).<br /> <b>REVISED</b><br /> <b>Skills</b>: Crafts, Drive, Etiquette, Firearms<br /> <b>Knowledges</b>: Computer, Law, Linguistics, Politics, Science<br /> <br /> <b>W20<br /> Skills:</b> Crafts, Drive, Etiquette, Firearms, Larceny<br /> <b>Knowledges</b>: Academics, Computer, Law, Science, Technology </div> </div> </div>Seems maybe a little few, that these abilities aren't available, but still as many dots are allowed to be spend. But, well, that is the rules.<br /> <br /> As for all the actions that don't require rolls: I usually tend to think Lupus don't know some very fundamental things, but they have the ability to figure them out, or get them explained. Lupus have had a couple of month, or maybe years from first change to Rite of Passage. And while homid garou might need to come to understand their new instincts and body language reading skills, lupus have time to get a bit understanding for homid garou and humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T07:40:17-07:00","id":946931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=946879#post946879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But do Lupus-born have high stats in a lot of these because they're lupus, or do they have high stats because they still get full ability dots and have nowhere else to put them? I can't help but wonder how much of this thought process was reverse-engineered from a decade or two of gameplay.<br /> <br /> Remember with dots- a little goes a long way. Sure, wolves are faster than humans. That's why that form gets bonus physical attributes and a x2 running modifier. So a wolf that runs a lot shouldn't be sporting significantly more athletics than a human that runs a lot. Same for Brawl. Does a handful of territorial disputes and dominance displays over the course of 2 years of life really put the lupus on par with a professional boxer or MMA fighter in homid form? It's a big deal to have more than 2 dots in an ability... a 3 is a level of competence on par with a Master's Degree or a seasoned professional. A 4 means someone is as good at something as you're likely to meet in a normal person's life, because 5 is an olympic-level, 'one of the best on the planet'-scale ability.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But a big questions is &quot;How much intelligence is that worth?&quot; Even assuming most Garou can't/don't finish High School, does the first change impart a Lupus with something actually comparable to 8 hours of education a day, 180+ days a year, for 10-12 years? Sure, we know Lupus can't start with Drive or Firearms or Computers/Technology/etc without spending freebie points... But can they do multiplication? Do they know what bacteria are, how longitude works, that there are seven continents, what lightning is, or what a kidney does? Homid-born from developed nations are sporting somewhere in the vicinity of 15,000 hours of education on very fundamental things that weren't considered even remotely obvious as little as a few centuries ago, and there is so much more to a Homid upbringing than simply understanding the nuances of human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>A starting Character does not necissarily represent someone who has just gone the Change. they could have been training for years. A starting Homid could be anything from a 12 yearold to a 35 yearold.. the 35 yearold does not get more points for the 23 more years of life experience. Lets look at Kinfolk they in all ways get fewer points.. even though they have an easier time fitting into society and can easily be college graduates, military men etc. Yet.. fewer points.<br /> <br /> Points have nothing to do with an attempt at simulation and more to do with starting all the players on the same page. Now if you feel that the benefit of Gnosis out weighs the in ability to start with a few things then by all means add more bonuses to playing Homid, but honestly most people do not agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T07:50:03-07:00","id":946939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=946879#post946879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember with dots- a little goes a long way. Sure, wolves are faster than humans. That's why that form gets bonus physical attributes and a x2 running modifier. So a wolf that runs a lot shouldn't be sporting significantly more athletics than a human that runs a lot. Same for Brawl. Does a handful of territorial disputes and dominance displays over the course of 2 years of life really put the lupus on par with a professional boxer or MMA fighter in homid form? It's a big deal to have more than 2 dots in an ability... a 3 is a level of competence on par with a Master's Degree or a seasoned professional. A 4 means someone is as good at something as you're likely to meet in a normal person's life, because 5 is an olympic-level, 'one of the best on the planet'-scale ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slight nitpick, but 3 being a Master's Degree is only for Knowledges. In Talents/Skills 2 is &quot;Practiced&quot; and 3 is &quot;Competent&quot;. <br /> And yes, I would argue that it is easy to justify a wolf having more Athletics than a &quot;human who runs a lot&quot; since the wolf does so almost everyday, for hours, for survival. In the wild, a non athletic wolf probably died. It is certainly possible to write up a professional runner who starts with more dots in Athletics. It's just that on average, a Lupus should have more than a Homid. Same with Survival, Primal Urge, Alertness and possibly a few other skills. <br /> I'm not saying that Lupus should start out with 4-5s in these skills for no reason. Just that having 2-3 in the core survival skills isn't remotely odd.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T13:20:50-07:00","id":947194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=946939#post946939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Slight nitpick, but 3 being a Master's Degree is only for Knowledges. In Talents/Skills 2 is &quot;Practiced&quot; and 3 is &quot;Competent&quot;.<br /> And yes, I would argue that it is easy to justify a wolf having more Athletics than a &quot;human who runs a lot&quot; since the wolf does so almost everyday, for hours, for survival. In the wild, a non athletic wolf probably died. It is certainly possible to write up a professional runner who starts with more dots in Athletics. It's just that on average, a Lupus should have more than a Homid. Same with Survival, Primal Urge, Alertness and possibly a few other skills.<br /> I'm not saying that Lupus should start out with 4-5s in these skills for no reason. Just that having 2-3 in the core survival skills isn't remotely odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of like the Realm and Lookshy Dragon-Blooded Ability requirements, only without the additional Ability dots (so, more like the ultra-irritating &quot;Lunars must have this many dots in Survival and one in a combat Ability, no compensation!). If you're low on them, you have some explaining to do. How much explaining depends on how extensive your character's shortcomings are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T21:10:33-07:00","id":947466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=946819#post946819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is said, that the human-like intelligence explodes in their minds after the first change. From that point on, several garou traits are active that weren't before. Healing, shape shifting, stepping sideways and ageing like a human.<br /> So, lupus born garou (and to a lesser degree metis born) were garou all their live, but developed into adolescence rather rapidly.<br /> <br /> So, the human-like intelligence doesn't develop over 2 or 3 years, but really in an instant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, they develop human like intelligence and so have the ability to learn like a human. Though what they don't have is human-like knowledge. For example, their vocabulary in human languages is very close to zero. Learning a language can take years and mastering the basics of human society enough to have even the most simple interaction with a human would probably take a few years as well. I'm not talking about knowing who fought in WWII or what a cell is, I mean just the most basic aspects of human communication that even a stone age human child would know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T22:04:52-07:00","id":947501,"title":"","content":"Magic? I mean, that is why they cannot learn certain Abilities without spending freebie points, the ancient magic that creates them has not been adjusted in 15,000 years or so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T23:30:23-07:00","id":947560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=947466#post947466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes, they develop human like intelligence and so have the ability to learn like a human. Though what they don't have is human-like knowledge. For example, their vocabulary in human languages is very close to zero. Learning a language can take years and mastering the basics of human society enough to have even the most simple interaction with a human would probably take a few years as well. I'm not talking about knowing who fought in WWII or what a cell is, I mean just the most basic aspects of human communication that even a stone age human child would know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought they magically got a local tongue. Oh well its not like they are planning to make a book on.. oh wait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:26:45-07:00","id":947583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=947466#post947466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, yes, they develop human like intelligence and so have the ability to learn like a human. Though what they don't have is human-like knowledge. For example, their vocabulary in human languages is very close to zero. Learning a language can take years and mastering the basics of human society enough to have even the most simple interaction with a human would probably take a few years as well. I'm not talking about knowing who fought in WWII or what a cell is, I mean just the most basic aspects of human communication that even a stone age human child would know.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. It is explicitly stated with the breed description, that language is a weakness to lupus, however no mechanics are given.<br /> As for inter-human basic behaviour I disagree. As a lupus the character has still learned some inter-species behaviour and can adapt certain aspects of wolf behaviour to human interaction. Meaning without knowing the uniform of a cop the lupus can still discern that the person has some kind of authority due to the reactions of others towards the cop, as well as the cop's bearing and mannerisms. Such is not without fail, but this is where empathy, primal-urge and the strangely enough not limited Streetwise augment the wits and intelligence levels the lupus character has.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure how long it takes to learn basic forms of language. A two year old toddler learns about 10 words a day and can form basic sentences. A suddenly human-minded lupus however has the mind of an adolescent not a toddlers (well, assuming two dots which is human average according to the books). That said, the lupus doesn't forget what he witnessed before the First Change, so he can re-evaluate human speech he heard before his mind developed. Even though, the lupus is akin to someone who is visiting, working and living in a land where a foreign language is spoken. Depending on the language, one can be a decent speaker within 6 month under this conditions (I googled that).<br /> <br /> Within the confines of the game mechanics, one could deny a lupus a mother tongue and have him learn English as a foreign language. Before W20, that was a linguistics dot, worth 3XP. So, after one month of training the teacher would roll Manipulation + Instructions versus 11 minus the Intelligence of the student. So, assuming stats of 2, in each trait. So according to some internet oWoD probability charts such a roll has still 1.4 successes on average, so after on average three roll (and three months) the are three successes accumulated, allowing for three XP to be spend and therefore learn the language.<br /> No idea how W20 handles this, since it is a merit now, but that would be revied Editons mechanic-wise take on learning the language.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind, that all garou cliath are taught Garou Tongue, which doesn't count as foreign language and the process of learning it is brushed over, really.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T01:57:02-07:00","id":947611,"title":"","content":"I've been toying around with the idea with character creation of Merits. A character has to buy Homid/Lupus/Metis as a Flawrit (Merit and Flaw, similar to buying race as a merit in Shadowrun) that comes with a &quot;starter kit&quot; in terms of Abilities, Gnosis and a few other stuff. Same thing for Auspice and Tribe. The idea is that these flawrits would be mandatory and mechanicly equal towards each other. While some gives bonus to some traits they have restrictions or penalties on certain other traits.<br /> <br /> Problem is i started with this idea for Vampire, with the default being Caitiff and the Merits representing Clan and what traits you get for being of the specific Clan. The thing is there is no &quot;default&quot; type of Garou. Sure you can be Ronin, but you HAVE to have a Breed and Auspice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T07:28:52-07:00","id":947752,"title":"","content":"I have had good experiences with a system where you buy all your traits with XP. We have, depending on Auspice, maximum and minimum ranges for Rage and based on Breed for Gnosis, but it is not that limiting as having Gnosis 1 (plus freebies) for homid, period.<br /> <br /> So, tribe, auspice and breed only change your gift lists, and tribal weakness. The latter isn't really level between the tribes, but neither are their gift lists equal, so....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T08:05:10-07:00","id":947780,"title":"","content":"I prefer just to give a Lupus a native language. We are talking about magically giving an animal human intelligence, as well as everything else associated with being a Garou, so magically imprinting a language is really nothing by comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:25:56-07:00","id":948507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/945204-honestly-though-should-all-things-be-equal-homid-born?p=947780#post947780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer just to give a Lupus a native language. We are talking about magically giving an animal human intelligence, as well as everything else associated with being a Garou, so magically imprinting a language is really nothing by comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to Garou Tongue, that is hand waived to any character after the Rite of Passage (but is a foreign language for Kin).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}